From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 06:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: cache scanned HI16 originals

Multiple LO16 relocations can share one LUI. If the first LO16 patches
that LUI and the second LO16 later finds it by backward scanning, reading
the live instruction reconstructs an already-relocated absolute address.

Remember the original LUI as soon as scanning discovers it so later LO16
relocations reuse the unpatched instruction.
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
index 483f6b0..0afc38e 100644
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
@@ -93,8 +93,10 @@ static inline int flat_mips_find_hi16_for_lo16(u32 __user *rp, u32 lo,
 			continue;
 
 		*hi_rp = (__force u32 __user *)scan;
-		if (!flat_mips_lookup_hi16(*hi_rp, hi_insn))
+		if (!flat_mips_lookup_hi16(*hi_rp, hi_insn)) {
 			*hi_insn = insn;
+			flat_mips_remember_hi16(*hi_rp, insn);
+		}
 		return 1;
 	}
 
